  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of dizziness and giddiness accompanied by a history of transient cerebral ischemic attacks and known sick sinus syndrome (diagnosis codes G42.4, I49.5, R42). Mobile cardiac telemetry (CPT 93229) is ordered to correlate these symptomatic events with potential arrhythmic activity or conduction abnormalities that may not be captured on standard ambulatory monitoring. SilverBridge Advantage denied the claim under Reason Code CO-197, indicating that the required precertification or prior authorization was not obtained before services were rendered; this appeal requests reconsideration of the medical necessity determination for this diagnostic monitoring service."
